\tr{\td{Mask contract "superset, deterministic"; \code{\verb~|CODE~} as a hint through the node's \code{\verb~|c~} word; \code{\verb~|LAZYD~} writes into the caller's frame; overlay arrays reloaded after \code{\verb~|blockRoot~}; one rule for throwables; work packages named M1-M8}\td{2.4, 2.6, 3.3, 1.3, 12 R4, R11, 13}\td{C1.14}}
\tr{\td{Pair keys ordered unsigned; unbound constant nodes decline; \code{\verb~|GET~} bounds-checked in all builds; every let value is a LET suspension}\td{1.5, 2.4, 2.8, 4.2, 9}\td{C3.14 (5-8)}}
\tr{\td{Staging re-sequenced with measured gates and CPU targets; v0 tables every node; platform gate at the first Init acceptance}\td{11}\td{C2.7, C2.2, C1.15, C1.11}}
\tr{\td{Host convention decided: convention H, depth bound 64 (\code{\verb~|review/stepper-convention.md~}); frames exist only when a judgment is suspended; \code{\verb~|ACT~} registers in a register stack; \code{\verb~|TRY~} written only on suspension, without \code{\verb~|tryp~}; operations that call sub-judgments get frame ops; trace = \code{\verb~|call~} events}\td{1.3 (last paragraph), 8.2 "Decision", 13.3, 13.4, 13.7}\td{B4 decision; skeleton, 2026-11-24}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|MISS = 0x7FFFFFFC~} instead of -1 (which is the immediate 2^31 - 1); \code{\verb~|TSTAMP PERM = 0x3FFFFFFF~} instead of 0x7FFFFFFF (which is the signal SUSP); run header bit positions fixed; FVAR memo word \code{\verb~|M_FV0~}; \code{\verb~|Hash~} as part of the frozen table format; signals, staging switches and debug bits in \code{\verb~|Op~}}\td{13.3, 13.7}\td{inconsistencies found while the constants were written into \code{\verb~|Layout~} / \code{\verb~|Op~} (skeleton)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} = 128 instead of 64: on Init the machine wrote 0.234\% of its call events as frames under D = 64 (bound of convention H12 item 2: 0.1\%), 0.041\% under 128, 0.017\% under 256, with identical ticks, call events and outcomes; CPU time on Init does not distinguish 64 from 256 (arena-shaped container, two rounds). Record limit 2^27 per session (one \code{\verb~|int[]~}), array growth guarded against the Java heap (\code{\verb~|E_MEM~}), \code{\verb~|Machine.vbase~} / \code{\verb~|rbase~} for \code{\verb~|poison~}, the machine's own \code{\verb~|NatStore~} overlay, run-header bit \code{\verb~|RUN_OPEN~}, frame op \code{\verb~|LSTEP 0x3C~}}\td{13.3, 9, 1.6, 2.9 (\src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M6.md} F1, F16-F22)}\td{M6 and requests of M1, M4, M8, 2026-11-24}}
\tr{\td{Module as built: files \code{\verb~|Hash~}, \code{\verb~|Scope~}, \code{\verb~|Show~}; file ownership per package with the sandbox workflow; entry steps as the interface between packages; fixture language; \code{\verb~|rlvm-testkit~} as a test dependency}\td{13.1, 13.7}\td{skeleton, 2026-11-24}}
\tr{\td{\strong{Eager reduction (wave 6, 2026-11-24)}: 5.2 and 5.3 say that conversion does not depend on the declaration being checked, and 5.4 lets \code{\verb~|POS~} be read while \code{\verb~|ER~} is set. Both are wrong where \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~} is involved: eager reduction is a MODE of the official \code{\verb~|is_def_eq~} (a pair can be T plain and F under ER, and the reverse), and the official success cache lives for one declaration and is keyed by terms with unique free variables, while the pair table and the memo words are keyed by canonical values and outlive binder scopes and (warm) declarations. Rule as built: a declaration that enters eager reduction is DECLINED by the facade in every configuration (\code{\verb~|Machine.enterER~}, \code{\verb~|erSeen~}; \code{\verb~|E_LIMIT~} / \code{\verb~|UNSUPPORTED_INPUT~}), the reference engine decides it. To take such declarations back: mode-tagged pair entries plus memo words that record whether a K-rule comparison was involved, or unique variables per \code{\verb~|OPEN~} in a session of their own}\td{4.4.1 c0, 4.5.4, 5.2, 5.3, 5.4, 14.2}\td{findings M6-F26, S-F4, S-F5 (arena \code{\verb~|bad/bugs/rec-of-subst-prop~}); \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M6.md} F26}}
\tr{\td{Session cap: the machine has a cap of its own (\code{\verb~|-X machine.session-kib~}, default 1 MiB) beside the driver's; pooled session arrays (kept slabs, pair tables, working stacks); growth allocations never raise \code{\verb~|OutOfMemoryError~}}\td{1.6, 9, 14.5}\td{measured: CPU time rises with the cap while instructions fall (NOTES-M6 F24, F25, F27)}}
\tr{\td{Switches: lists read left to right (\code{\verb~|none~}, \code{\verb~|default~}, \code{\verb~|all~}, \code{\verb~|-name~}); two experiment bits per package; \code{\verb~|t2~}, \code{\verb~|lazyeval~}, \code{\verb~|levels-complete~}, \code{\verb~|match~}, \code{\verb~|joint~}, \code{\verb~|same~}; \src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md} is the list of record. Run header bits 4..7 = count of non-HOLE slots (M1)}\td{11, 13.3, 2.4}\td{wave 6 (NOTES-M6 F28, F29)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{Integration of wave 6 (2026-11-24)}: the machine was the default engine from 19:41Z to 20:35Z (\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} = 100) and is not any more (10): findings E1-F1 .. E1-F5, wrong accepts against the official checker because INFER types a bound variable by what its slot holds (4.5: the let rule, INST of a re-inferred redex, CBIND's comparison variable, B9) instead of by the binder's declared type - to be fixed before it is the default again. Its default switch set is \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,bodies,pchk,match,joint,code,casetrees,lazycases,directrules,lazyeval,same~}, cap 1 MiB, host depth bound 128, the Truffle tier off (\src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md} has the gate and the measurement of every choice). \code{\verb~|KVAL~} (4.2): the inline cache of a site is filled also when the value arrives through a frame (the frame's \code{\verb~|dst~} names the site; finding M8-F1: without it the tick count depended on the host depth bound). 3.3 "Finding the block of a closure": the hint in a binder node's \code{\verb~|c~} word is state of the STORE, so it assumes ONE code store (one machine engine) per store; a hint of another code store is rejected by the validation and the closure is walked (found in the gate's harness, whose lanes are engines of their own)}\td{3.3, 4.2, 8.2, 11}\td{integrator of wave 6}}
\tr{\td{Unchanged in substance: value kinds and canonical free variables, the instruction tables and transitions of section 4 apart from the rows named above, check stamps (5.3), the worked examples (instruction estimates), the reuse verdict (section 10)}\td{}\td{not contested}}
}

\p{Not resolved in this document, by design: (the choice between the two host conventions was resolved on 2026-11-24, see 8.2 "Decision"); CPU-time profiles of the Cedar-level corpora (\code{\verb~|R13~} counts instructions); the session cap and \code{\verb~|ELAB_AT~} (sweeps of section 11); the two store accessors marked "requested" in section 12.}
}
